2. In this Order —
“aggregate duration where permissible noise levels are exceeded”, in relation to any period, means an aggregate duration of occasions in the exempted sessions of that period when the noise levels emitted from the relevant premises exceed the permissible noise levels;
“Boundary Noise Limits Regulations” means the Environmental Protection and Management (Boundary Noise Limits for Factory Premises) Regulations (Rg 1);
“exempted session” means any of the following:
(a)between 12 a.m. and 6.59 a.m. of any day;
(b)between 7 p.m. and 11.59 p.m. of any day;
“permissible noise levels” means the maximum permissible noise levels prescribed in regulation 3(1)(b), subject to regulation 3(3), of the Boundary Noise Limits Regulations;
“relevant premises” means the factory premises located at 3 Meranti Road, Singapore 628536;
“specified 12‑month period” means the period starting from 1 July 2025 and ending on 30 June 2026 (both dates inclusive) and each subsequent period of 12 months starting on 1 July of a year and ending on 30 June of the succeeding year.
